{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q2210953","formula":"C₅H₄O₃","hill":"C5H4O3","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":5.0,"H":4.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"2-furoic acid","ru":"Пирослизевая кислота"},"descriptions":{"en":"2-Furoic acid is an organic compound, consisting of a furan ring and a carboxylic acid side-group. Along with other furans, its name is derived from the Latin word furfur, meaning bran, from which these compounds were first produced. The salts and esters of furoic acids are known as furoates.","ru":"Пирослизевая кислота — 2-фуранкарбоновая кислота, бесцветные иглы или листочки, плохо растворима в воде (при 0 °С — 2,7 %, при 100 °С — 25 %), растворяется в спирте и эфире. Температура плавления составляет 133 °C, при 100 °C возгоняется. Ультрафиолетовый спектр: максимальная длина волны — 243 нм."},"fame":15,"pubchemCid":6919,"mass":112.08,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=COC(=C1)C(=O)O","inchikey":"SMNDYUVBFMFKNZ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"furan-2-carboxylic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"6919","atoms":12,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.698,"y":1.1,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":2.08,"y":-1.167,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":2.114,"y":1.106,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":0.021,"y":-0.053,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.816,"y":-1.145,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.134,"y":-0.629,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.009,"y":0.74,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":1.441,"y":0.048,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.522,"y":-2.185,"z":-0.001,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.059,"y":-1.187,"z":0.0,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.717,"y":1.556,"z":0.0,"el":"H"},{"x":3.056,"y":-1.062,"z":0.001,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,3,1],[0,6,1],[1,7,1],[1,11,1],[2,7,2],[3,4,2],[3,7,1],[4,5,1],[4,8,1],[5,6,2],[5,9,1],[6,10,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2210953","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"descri